ss function boundaries and may omit memory aliasing, call side effects, or unresolved indirect flow.","Memory read/write effects include stack and temporary memory operations; they do not identify persistent state or business meaning.","Operation, input, and def-use limits can truncate large functions; inspect truncation, omitted lower bounds, and known omitted counts before drawing conclusions.","Known omitted-edge counts cover links omitted from retained operations; omitted operations may contain additional uncounted links."]},"facet_availability":{"pseudocode":{"available":true},"assembly":{"available":true},"comments":{"available":true},"callers":{"available":true},"callees":{"available":true},"references":{"available":true},"strings_names":{"available":true},"cfg":{"available":true}},"limitations":["Unresolved computed or indirect flows without target addresses are not represented as reference edges.","Thunk and external classifications are Ghidra FunctionManager observations; they do not resolve targetless calls.","Pseudocode and assembly are Ghidra-specific representations, not original source or Hopper-equivalent text.","Synthetic Ghidra entry-point references without actionable memory sources are omitted."]},"confidence":"observed","authority":"shipped-artifact","environment":null,"limitations":["The session serves operations only after Ghidra reports default auto-analysis complete; incomplete analysis does not expose partial results.","The imported Program and temporary project are ephemeral and deleted on close. Annotation operations edit session database metadata; original executable bytes are never written.","Cancelling an active Ghidra request terminates its ephemeral database and discards session annotations. The selected target remains open; the next provider query imports the original artifact again.","Default-space addresses use lowercase 0x-prefixed hexadecimal; other address spaces use <percent-encoded-space>:0x<hex>.","References cover the compl